CORE
main.c
--unwind 6 --unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ assertion k == 4: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ assertion r\.s\.is_long == 0: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^\[main\.unwind\.0\]
--
A bit field of one union member, read after byte updates of other bytes
(memmove into the data array), was not simplified to the value written, so
the loop bound n stayed symbolic: symbolic execution produced an unwinding
assertion, and without --unwind did not terminate.  libc++'s alternate
std::string layout (Apple arm64) keeps the short size there, and every
string comparison became an unbounded memcmp on macOS 14.
